{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-3X+1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-32321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-3X+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-3X+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}-3A+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}-3A+I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10-(-6)+1 & 6-18 \\\\ 1-3 & 15-9+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-32321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4ae49595829175660b1502c00b26bf0914a802c4abdc6047b3e066dc3a8be17"} {"question" "q-32321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-32321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}17 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}17 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}22 & -8 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ -11 & 17\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-32321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}17 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $U=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, then ${U}^{3}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to find ${U}^{2},$ we multiply $U$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{2} & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${U}^{3}={U}^{2}\\cdot U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{3} & ={U}^{2}\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4ae49595829175660b1502c00b26bf0914a802c4abdc6047b3e066dc3a8be17"} {"question" "q-130582" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130582" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 24\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130582" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}].$  Find $f(D)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-4 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-4I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)={D}^{2}-4I.$ \n\nLet's calculate ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & ={D}^{2}-4I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-4 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & 4-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" 