" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-X+5 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-X+5I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(C)={C}^{2}-C+5I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(C):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(C) & ={C}^{2}-C+5I \\\\  & =C-C+5I \\\\  & =5I \\\\  & =5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4ae49595829175660b1502c00b26bf0914a802c4abdc6047b3e066dc3a8be17"} {"question" "q-130687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-130687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-279430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $F=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find ${F}^{3}.$\n\n| ${F}^{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5cb92da65af506757eb99598"} {"question" "q-279430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to find ${F}^{2},$ we multiply $F$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{2} & =F\\cdot F \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${F}^{3}={F}^{2}\\cdot F,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{3} & ={F}^{2}\\cdot F \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 36 \\\\ 18 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97e20811f88f3eb6f06af456ba5fe11dfff31af5c